"An earlier lesson in this unit distinguished excess heat from deficient heat — one caused by too much yang, the other by too little yin. Cold works the same way, in reverse, and deserves the same careful separation. Yang deficiency is a shortage: yang itself has grown too weak to warm the body properly, the way a fire that's been allowed to die down produces less heat than before. This kind of cold tends to be constant, accompanied by visibly pale skin, a preference for warm drinks and warm weather, and a general low energy that matches the qi deficiency covered earlier in this course.": "15648457812e",
"An earlier lesson in this unit distinguished excess heat from deficient heat — one caused by too much yang, the other by too little yin. Cold works the same way, in reverse, and deserves the same careful separation. Yang deficiency is a shortage: yang itself has grown too weak to warm the body properly, the way a fire that's been allowed to die down produces less heat than before. This kind of cold tends to be constant, accompanied by visibly pale skin, a preference for warm drinks and warm weather, and a general low energy that matches the qi deficiency covered earlier in this course. Yin excess works by addition rather than subtraction: yin itself — the cooling, condensing substance — has become too abundant, overwhelming yang's warming function even though yang itself may be perfectly adequate. This kind of cold tends to feel heavier and more localized, often described as an oppressive coldness in a specific area, sometimes with visible fluid retention or swelling, since excess yin also tends to bring an excess of the fluid it's associated with. The response, once again, runs in opposite directions. Yang deficiency calls for warming and strengthening yang directly, the way a fire needs more fuel. Yin excess calls for draining or transforming the excess substance itself, the way a flooded room needs drainage rather than a stronger heater. Confusing the two — warming a room that's actually flooded, or trying to drain a room that's simply lost its heat source — repeats the same error this unit already warned against for heat, just with the temperature running the other way.": "7d8eb668f60c",
